PROPOSED PATCH - UNTESTED ON GPU.
Pass the model's swiglu_limit (stored by FusedMoE on the RoutedExperts layer) to the B12x planner of
the rank-sliced / projection-mixed EXL3 runtime (TPMoEScratchCaps.swiglu_limit, which B12x threads into
the projection-mixed Trellis launch) and to the expert-mixed Trellis compiler (compile_mixed_trellis's
swiglu_limit argument). Upstream vLLM's FusedMoE receives swiglu_limit for this model
(models/glm5next/common/model.py); upstream has no vendored EXL3 path, so there is no upstream patch
to port. Against the 0.9.1 package; applies with `patch -p1` from the directory that contains vllm/.
Checked on CPU only (applies; static plumbing check, see expected/). Not run on a GPU: whether the
kernels apply the clamp as the vLLM reference does, and any output, accuracy or speed effect, are not
measured. The runtime cache keys do not include the limit; all layers of this model share one value.

--- a/vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/exl3.py
+++ b/vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/exl3.py
@@ -2751,6 +2751,7 @@
                 force_tile_config=mixed["tile_config"],
                 rotation_input_dtype=("bf16" if x.dtype == torch.bfloat16 else "fp16"),
                 route_ids_dtype=topk_ids.dtype,
+                swiglu_limit=getattr(layer, "swiglu_limit", None),
             )
             return {
                 "capacity": capacity,
@@ -2966,6 +2967,9 @@
                     if bf16_epilogue
                     else torch.float32
                 ),
+                # Routed-expert SwiGLU clamp from the model config
+                # (swiglu_limit); FusedMoE stores it on the layer.
+                swiglu_limit=getattr(layer, "swiglu_limit", None),
                 **mixed_launch_caps,
             )
             plan = api.plan(caps)
